      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_140",
        on: "new_turn",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("You know I am here to claim the Sceptre as my birthright, Li’sar. Is your hatred so great that you would rather chase after us than even <b><i>try</i></b> to save Wesnoth from the ruin it has fallen to at the hands of your mother?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:clear_shroud",
            side: 1,
            xs: "",
            ys: "",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:lift_fog",
            side: 1,
            cells: "",
            radius: 2,
            multiturn: "no",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lisar",
            portrait: "portraits/lisar-mad.webp",
            text: _("I <i>am</i> trying to save it — from you. Do you have any idea how much chaos you and your little gang of ruffians have caused?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("Asheviere took control of Wesnoth with violence, and violence has filled every part of her reign. All she knows is blood! And all she cares about is power."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lisar",
            text: _("You really are just a child. Maybe the Aethenwood runs on friendship and flowers, but here in the real world sometimes people get hurt. And yes, sometimes that means unsavory decisions, like the kind the queen has to make every day."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            portrait: "portraits/konrad-$konrad_portrait_base-mad.webp",
            text: _("Perhaps you truly think you’re acting for the best. But know this: with me today stand free peoples from all corners of Wesnoth, united as one against the tyranny of Asheviere. Whether we defeat you now or never, Wesnoth will never stop fighting for what is right!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:delay",
            time: 500,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lisar",
            text: _("... not bad, as hero speeches go. We’ll see how the palace dungeons change your tune."),
          },
          {
